                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1355: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-02T16:00:00+08:00">May 2, 1935—4 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 2—6:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. Legation’s 177, May 1, 3 p.m., second and third paragraphs.</p>
                <p>Cunningham reports that he has discussed the matter with the Minister and
                    proposes to attempt to arrange for the inclusion of equal rights.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
